    "why_unexplained_rather_than_standard_dipper": {
      "1_bimodal_amplitude_and_symmetric_bursts": "Classical Class II inner-disk dippers (Cody et al. 2014; Ansdell et al. 2016) exhibit 0.1-0.8 mag extinction dips below a flat photospheric ceiling (asymmetry M > +0.5). ZTF18aaxioyg spans 1.7751 mag (zg) and 1.7779 mag (zr) peak-to-peak, combining +1.4571 mag (73.87% flux drop) deep fades below strict median with -0.5866 mag (+71.6% flux surge) brightening bursts above the all-clean median (16.6764 vs 17.2630 in zg; 15.4186 vs 15.9930 in zr; Gskew = +0.385/+0.399).",
      "2_super_rayleigh_dimming_and_reddening_when_brighter_inversion": "Across 49 same-night zg+zr pairs (baseline median zg-zr = 1.0851 mag), the top 3 fades show selective dimming slopes d(zg)/d(zr) = 1.464, 1.435, and 1.475 \u2014 steeper than both standard R_V=3.1 ISM dust (A_g/A_r = 1.31) and evolved large-grain Class II inner-disk dippers (d(g)/d(r) ~ 1.05-1.25). Conversely, during the MJD 59883.17 outburst (zg=16.6968, zr=15.5644), the star reddens while brightening (d_zg = -0.2976 vs d_zr = -0.3449 mag, zg-zr = 1.1324 mag, +0.0473 mag redder than median), contradicting both magnetospheric accretion hotspots (bluer when brighter) and simple dust-screen clearing.",
      "3_no_keplerian_corotation_period_and_multi_scale_mhps": "Unlike inner-disk warp dippers locked at P ~ 2-10 d, ALeRCE finds only diurnal cadence aliases (Period_band_1 = 0.0556 d, Period_band_2 = 0.9959 d, Psi_eta = 1.90/1.64), while Mexican-Hat Power Spectrum ratios (MHPS_ratio = 3.79 in zg, 4.10 in zr; MHPS_low_365_2 = 30.77 vs MHPS_high_30_2 = 9.29) indicate dominant 100-365 d outer-disk modulation superposed with GP_DRW_tau = 1.55-2.67 d stochastic collapses.",
      "4_uncataloged_across_surveys": "Despite 924 ZTF epochs, Gaia DR3 lists phot_variable_flag = NOT_AVAILABLE (while 5 stars within 120 arcsec are flagged VARIABLE), with 0 entries in SIMBAD, VSX, or published Cygnus YSO dipper catalogs, and conflicting ALeRCE rank-1 classes (YSO 0.74-0.99 in 11 LC classifiers vs CV/Nova in 2 beta LC classifiers, EA/CEP in periodic classifiers, and AGN/VS in stamp classifiers)."
    }
